	<ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id='F172' contextRef='C1'>&lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;text-align:justify'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;NATURE OF OPERATIONS AND SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Business&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt; - RH energytrans, LLC (RH), was granted a 7(c) certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity to convert, construct and operate an interstate pipeline extending from an interconnection with Tennessee Gas Pipeline Company (TGP) in Meadville, PA to an interconnection with Dominion East Ohio (DEO) in Ashtabula, Ohio (the &amp;#147;Risberg Project&amp;#148;) by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) at the end of 2018.&amp;#160; RH originally owned 28 miles of 12-inch pipeline and has added approximately 4 miles of existing 8 inch and 28 miles of new 12-inch pipeline in Pennsylvania and Ohio. The construction and operation of this interstate pipeline is regulated by the FERC&lt;font style='color:red'&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;The Risberg Project provides much needed access to natural gas supply to the Ashtabula, County area to ensure system reliability and enhance future commercial business development.&amp;#160; RH offers both firm and interruptible transportation services.&amp;#160; DEO is the anchor customer having executed a Precedent Agreement with RH for 40,000 Dekatherms per day of firm capacity (approximately 73% of RH&amp;#146;s total initial capacity of 55,000 Dekatherms per day) at a fixed rate per Dekatherm per day for a term of 15 years, with an option to extend service under then applicable tariff rates for up to an additional 10 years.&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Organizational &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;&amp;#150; The Company, a Limited Liability Company under the laws of the State of Delaware, was formed on February 15, 2017..&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0in;line-height:115%;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Cash&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt; &amp;#150; At December 31, 2025, the total of all the bank balances of all accounts was $532,173, $250,000 of which was covered by FDIC Insurance and $282,173 which was not. &amp;#160;At December 31, 2024, the total of all the bank balances of all accounts was $450,024, $250,000 of which was covered by FDIC Insurance and $200,024 which was not.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Cash Equivalents&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt; &amp;#150; The Company considers all highly liquid instruments purchased with an original maturity date of three months or less to be cash equivalents.&amp;#160; At December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company had no cash equivalents.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;text-indent:.5in'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Inventory&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt; &amp;#150; Inventory consists of construction supplies held for resale and is stated at the lower of cost or market, with cost determined on the first-in, first-out method.&amp;#160; As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company had no inventory balance.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;text-align:justify'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;text-align:justify'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Accounts Payable &amp;#150; Trade&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt; &amp;#150; As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company had an accounts payable balance of $1,077,330 and $894,321, respectively.&amp;#160; The balance consists of both project related costs and trade payables that will be paid in a timely manner based on agreements with specific vendors.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Risberg Line Project Costs&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt; &amp;#150; Project costs to date are stated at cost and have been evaluated for proper capitalization using FASB standards.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;text-indent:.5in'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt; - For income tax purposes, the Company has elected to be treated as a partnership under the Internal Revenue Code (IRC).&amp;#160; Accordingly, the income and losses are passed through to its members, and no provision for federal income taxes has been included in these statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0in;line-height:115%;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;ENVIRONMENTAL COMMITMENTS AND CONTINGENCIES&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;Environmental Matters &amp;#150; The Company is subject to various federal, state, and local laws and regulations relating to the protection of the environment.&amp;#160; Although the Company believes that it is in material compliance with applicable environmental regulations, the risk of costs and liabilities are inherent in pipeline operation.&amp;#160; Liabilities for loss contingencies, including environmental remediation costs, arising from claims, assessments, litigation, fines, and penalties and other sources will be charged to expense when it is probable that a liability has been incurred and the amount of the assessment and/or remediation can be reasonably estimated.&amp;#160; There are no such liabilities reflected in the accompanying statements at December 31, 2025 and 2024.&amp;#160; However, the Company can provide no assurances that significant costs and liabilities will not be incurred in the future. Management is currently not aware of any material contingent liabilities that exist with respect to environmental matters.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0in;line-height:115%;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
