	<ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock id='F196' contextRef='C1'>&lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;RH energytrans, LLC (RH), was granted a 7(c) certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity to convert, construct and operate an interstate pipeline extending from an interconnection with Tennessee Gas Pipeline Company (TGP) in Meadville, PA to an interconnection with Dominion East Ohio (DEO) in Ashtabula, Ohio (the &amp;#147;Risberg Project&amp;#148;) by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) at the end of 2018.&amp;#160; RH originally owned 28 miles of 12-inch pipeline and has added approximately 4 miles of existing 8 inch and 28 miles of new 12-inch pipeline in Pennsylvania and Ohio. The construction and operation of this interstate pipeline is regulated by the FERC&lt;font style='color:red'&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin:0in;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;The Risberg Project provides much needed access to natural gas supply to the Ashtabula, County area to ensure system reliability and enhance future commercial business development.&amp;#160; RH offers both firm and interruptible transportation services.&amp;#160; DEO is the anchor customer having executed a Precedent Agreement with RH for 40,000 Dekatherms per day of firm capacity (approximately 73% of RH&amp;#146;s total initial capacity of 55,000 Dekatherms per day) at a fixed rate per Dekatherm per day for a term of 15 years, with an option to extend service under then applicable tariff rates for up to an additional 10 years. &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0in;line-height:107%;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0in;line-height:107%;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;'&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Times New Roman,serif'&gt;The pipeline facilities associated with the Risberg Line Project under Docket Number CP18-6-000 were authorized to be placed in service by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission on November 11, 2019. A Delegated Order authorizing the pipeline facilities to be placed into service was filed under Docket CP18-6-000 Accession Number 20191122-3031.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock>
